As an alternative solution to what Philippe posted, if you don't want
to pre-summarize your data, you can let geom_bar do that for you.

# bin is really a grouping, so should be a factor
dat$bin <- factor(dat$bin)

# the key idea you described (proportional bars) is provided by
position_fill()
ggplot(dat, aes(x=cl)) + geom_bar(aes(fill=bin), position="fill")

# Same thing, using qplot notation instead of ggplot notation
qplot(cl, data=dat, fill=bin, geom="bar", position="fill")

--Brian Diggs

