Hello,

I'm trying to make a faceted plot but I'm suffering from the problem
of having ugly data. I have a data frame I've dumped in from RMySQL,
and the column I want to facet on is a string. The problem is, the
column is in the format "FOO, BAR ..." (i.e. multiplicity is specified
in a string, terrible!).  So when I facet on that column, I might get
facets for FOO and BAR by themselves (which is what I do want) but I
also get facets for "FOO, BAR", "FOO, BAZ" etc.

I could somehow attempt to extract the information so that maybe
instead of string "FOO, BAR" I'd have a vector or array with both
"FOO" and "BAR" (help on this appreciated too). But even then, how
would I write an R formula that expresses that I want the graph
faceted by each individual "FOO", "BAR" etc?

Another approach would be one such that I would keep the data as it is
and somehow write a formula for qplot's facets= that would contain a
list of all the facets I want and then checks if each row's string
contains one of those facets? I don't know how the formula system
quite works.

Thanks,
~mali

P.S. Kudos to all the developers, this package has greatly simplified
my work.

